(6454736, 958107, 10785, '<td valign="top">Your second attempt got a lot of things right. The angle of the camera is better especially without the twisted horizon. The exposure is good and the PP is brighter with a wider range of highlights and shadows. A couple of things suffered in the second take such as the sharpness due to the camera shake. The blurred woman in the foreground is not a problem though as she is moving which adds to the dynamic feel.</td>', 'Your second attempt got a lot of things right. The angle of the camera is better especially without the twisted horizon. The exposure is good and the PP is brighter with a wider range of highlights and shadows. A couple of things suffered in the second take such as the sharpness due to the camera shake. The blurred woman in the foreground is not a problem though as she is moving which adds to the dynamic feel.', '2011-06-28 09:20:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(6454768, 957779, 117474, '<td valign="top">I thought this was a nice picture. And I gave it a 6. <br/>I don''t see the crop doing a whole bunch for it, though. I think with how the picture is flowing from right to left it might have benefitted from a crop omitting most of the foliage to the left (from about a third of the way from the left). That would give the photo a flowing composition <a href="//www.heatherowensphotography.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2010/09/goldenmean3.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">something like this</a> (rotated, of course) which is something I find very pleasing.<br/> <br/>It didn''t have much else that I could see to warrant giving it more marks, sorry :) Nice shot, as I said. And my views on it are completely personal, so you don''t have to agree with me! :D</td>', 'I thought this was a nice picture. And I gave it a 6. I don''t see the crop doing a whole bunch for it, though. I think with how the picture is flowing from right to left it might have benefitted from a crop omitting most of the foliage to the left (from about a third of the way from the left). That would give the photo a flowing composition something like this (rotated, of course) which is something I find very pleasing. It didn''t have much else that I could see to warrant giving it more marks, sorry :) Nice shot, as I said. And my views on it are completely personal, so you don''t have to agree with me! :D', '2011-06-28 10:30:01.000000', NULL, 1),
